.TH FACIAL-AUTH 1 "2026-11-17" "facial-auth 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
facial-auth \- manage face authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B facial-auth
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B facial-auth
links faces to user accounts and configures where a face may replace the
password (login screen, lock screen, sudo, su, polkit prompts).  The password
always remains available: a failed or skipped face scan never prevents a
classic login.
.PP
Linking a face to an account needs administrator rights.  The request is
authorised by polkit: the administrator is asked for their password
(graphically, or in the terminal through pkttyagent).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the state of the service, the camera and the accounts.
.TP
.B cameras
List detected cameras and whether they are infrared (IR) or colour (RGB).
.TP
.BR users " [\fILOGIN\fR]"
List the accounts the settings application offers (yours, the accounts that have faces or a session, the
ones named in \fBcore.extra_users\fR, and what the system enumerates), or look one account up by its login.
Directory accounts (LDAP, SSSD, Active Directory) are usually not enumerated: \fBfacial-auth users \fILOGIN\fR
shows whether the daemon can resolve one, which is what linking a face to it needs.
.TP
.BR list " [" \-u " \fIUSER\fR]"
List the faces linked to accounts.
.TP
.BR add " [" \-u " \fIUSER\fR] [" \-l " \fILABEL\fR] [" \-c " auto|ir|rgb] [" \-n " \fIN\fR]"
Take N photos (3 to 12, default 5) with the camera, guided by on-screen
instructions, then link the face to USER.
.TP
.BR import " [" \-u " \fIUSER\fR] [" \-l " \fILABEL\fR] \fIPHOTO\fR..."
Link a face from at least three photos, for instance taken with the Camera
application.
.TP
.BR remove " [" \-u " \fIUSER\fR] \fIID\fR, " clear " [" \-u " \fIUSER\fR]"
Remove one face, or every face of an account.  Users may always remove their own faces.
.TP
.BR enable ", " disable " [" \-u " \fIUSER\fR]"
Turn face authentication on or off for one account.
.TP
.BR test " [" \-c " auto|ir|rgb] [" \-\-liveness "]"
Check that the camera recognises you, head-turn test included.  When the head turn fails, says what
to change (turn further, less quickly...).  With \fB\-\-liveness\fR the measurements of the head turn
are printed (to tune \fBliveness.challenge_turn\fR).
.TP
.B check-camera
Check that the "infrared" camera does not see a phone screen (hold a phone showing a bright white page
close to the lens when asked).  A camera that passes is recorded as verified; services that require an
infrared camera only accept a verified one (\fBcamera.require_ir_check\fR).  Needs an administrator.
.TP
.BR service " [\fINAME\fR [any|ir|off]]"
Show or set where the face may be used, and which camera it requires.
.TP
.BR config " [\fIKEY\fR [\fIVALUE\fR]]"
Show or change a setting such as \fBrecognition.threshold\fR.
.TP
.BR fetch-models " [--from \fIDIR\fR]"
Download the face detection and recognition models (root).  Files are checked
against pinned SHA-256 sums.
.TP
.BR purge-orphans " [" \-n "] [" \-y "]"
Remove face data that no longer belongs to the account it was enrolled for (root).  Faces are filed
under the numeric user id but remember the account name they were enrolled for: when the account is
deleted and its id given to somebody else, or the account is renamed, they are ignored (nobody
inherits a face) and stay on disk until this command removes them.  \fB\-n\fR only lists them;
without \fB\-y\fR the command asks first.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose the installation and suggest fixes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/facial-auth/facial-auth.conf
Local configuration.  See \fI/usr/share/facial-auth/defaults.conf\fR.
.TP
.I /var/lib/facial-auth/
Face templates (embeddings only, never photographs), settings made from the settings application, and
\fIlockout.json\fR, the face lock-outs in progress (delete it, with the daemon stopped, to clear them).
.SH SECURITY
A colour webcam can be fooled by a photograph.  By default only an infrared
camera is trusted for sudo, su and polkit.  See
.I /usr/share/doc/facial-auth/SECURITY.md.gz
if installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pam_facial_auth (8),
.BR pam-auth-update (8),
.BR polkit (8)
